\ ==== stacks ====

1 dup . .
1 2 swap . .
1 2 over . . .
1 2 3 rot . . .
99 88 drop .s

clear
: dup-via-rs >r r@ r> ;
7 dup-via-rs . .
: store-fetch >r r> ;
42 store-fetch .
: peek-twice >r r@ r@ r> ;
9 peek-twice . . .

clear
1 2 nip . cr

\ pick copies the nth item from the top, leaving it in place; roll moves it
1 2 3 0 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 3
clear
1 2 3 1 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 2
clear
1 2 3 2 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 1
clear
1 2 3 2 roll .s cr              \ 2 3 1 — moved, not copied
clear
[ 100 200 300 ] [ 2 0 ] [: 2 pick swap @i :] map . cr   \ [ 300 100 ] — the array is reached below map's source
drop
\ a parked value is read by depth; the accumulator lives in fold-times, so no
\ word writes to a stack slot
10 20  0 [: drop 1 pick :] ' f+ 3 fold-times .s cr   \ 10 20 30 — 10 added three times
clear
[ 10 20 30 ] 0 [: 1 pick 1 pick @i nip :] ' f+ 2 fold-times nip . cr   \ 30 — elements 0 and 1
clear

1 2 3 3 pick                    \ (depth 3 with only 3 values below the count)
clear
1 2 -1 pick                     \ (negative depth)
clear
1 2 3 3 roll                    \ (depth 3 with only 3 values below the count)
clear
1 2 -1 roll                     \ (negative depth)
clear
0 [: :] -1 fold-times           \ (negative fold-times count)
clear
5 >side side-peek . side-depth . side-drop cr

clear

\ ==== clear gc ====

1 2 3 4 5 .s
clear .s
gc
1 .

clear
